* 2D mode 2 with direction 0 0: MOVCTL direction of die 2 (angle -90 -> (0,-1)) is used; same as ifd_m2_2d
* ORACLE (corrected after oracle run): token 2 = 0 -> area 0 %: the 2D root finder never converges (OBJPOS_interference.md 7.3, 100 steps): 'Object 2 to Object 1 interference positioning failed.', die 2 stays at +10. The MOVCTL fallback itself is checked by ifd_v_area1_dir0_2d (identical to ifd_m2_tol_2d).
KFREAD 0
SPIKE_SI.KEY
OBJPOS 2 1 0 10
OBJPOS 2 2 0.0 1 0 0 0
KFWRIT
OUT.KEY
